<title>SWEDEN: Astra says no FDA news on Pulmicort.</title>
<headline>Astra says no FDA news on Pulmicort.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish drugs company Astra said on Thursday it had not heard any news from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) about approval for its asthma treatment, the Pulmicort turbuhaler.</p>
<p>Brokers said market rumours that approval was imminent or even arrived was moving Astra's shares on the Stockholm bourse in Thursday trade,</p>
<p>At 1000 GMT Astra shares were trading four crowns higher at 134 crowns.  </p>
<p>&quot;We are not aware that anything has happened today,&quot; Astra spokesman Staffan Ternby told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;We think that the FDA investigation is in a positive stage and we think that it will be approved before the summer holidays.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
